{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Requests one more revision of the shutdown probe, this time to test the mechanism rather than the symptom. The corrected Fact says the strand comes from a buffered channel whose send stays selectable after the run loop has exited, while Barrier and Apply escape it only because applyCh is unbuffered by default. Config.BatchApplyCh exists precisely to buffer applyCh, and its own comment warns that it breaks the timeout guarantee on Apply, so enabling it should make Barrier and Apply strand exactly like VerifyLeader. The harness now records batch_apply_ch and adds three batched trials each for barrier and apply alongside the default and control cases, with comparisons separating the batched cases from the unbuffered ones. Its execution is requested; no observation is claimed until the receipt exists.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"batch_apply_ch_config\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":163,\\\"end_line\\\":174,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"b2ccc787c9384b008b5f9c668746f760-question-0\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"49fa455b2fe94d53ab6fed2fad19ce33-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The previous revision isolated the strand to VerifyLeader and attributed it to channel buffering. This revision adds BatchApplyCh cases that buffer applyCh for the Barrier and Apply call kinds, records batch_apply_ch in both events, and adds comparisons for the batched cases against the unbuffered defaults. The existing cases, event names and measured fields are unchanged.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_verify_future\\\",\\\"api_barrier_future\\\",\\\"api_apply_future\\\",\\\"defer_error_block\\\",\\\"verify_channel_buffer\\\",\\\"shutdown_close\\\",\\\"apply_channel_unbuffered\\\",\\\"batch_apply_ch_config\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run the shutdown probe for VerifyLeader, Barrier and Apply with the default unbuffered applyCh and again for Barrier and Apply with BatchApplyCh enabled, three trials each, recording how many futures are left incomplete in the racing phase and how many of eight post-shutdown calls are answered in the 500ms window, plus a no-shutdown control.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"BatchApplyCh is a supported configuration option whose documented effect is to buffer applyCh to MaxAppendEntries and to break the timeout guarantee on Apply.\\\",\n    \\\"Buffer size is MaxAppendEntries (the default), which is large enough that the eight post-shutdown sends never block, so the send case is selectable exactly as verifyCh's is.\\\",\n    \\\"Single-voter node, in-memory transport, 50ms timeouts, one process, as before.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"BatchApplyCh with BatchApplyChMaxAppendEntries or concurrency large enough to fill the buffer, and multi-node behaviour.\\\"]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case starts one real Raft instance with its own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, bootstrapped as a single Voter with HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 50ms and BatchApplyCh set only for the batched cases, and waits until it reports Leader. It emits assurance_shutdown_setup with the batch_apply_ch flag, issues 128 calls of the chosen kind from separate goroutines, each waiting on Error() with a 4000ms deadline, and in the shutdown cases calls Shutdown() from a goroutine 2ms later so the fill and the exit overlap. After Shutdown returns it issues 8 further calls of the same kind one at a time with a 500ms wait each, then emits assurance_shutdown_result with the racing counts, the post-phase counts and histograms, the shutdown error, the node state and the batch_apply_ch flag. The no-shutdown control never calls Shutdown. The harness is TestAssuranceShutdownFutureCompletion.\\\"),\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_setup\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"barrier\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batch_apply_ch\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Barrier with BatchApplyCh: at least one of eight post-shutdown calls left unanswered, which would show the strand follows the buffering rather than the API.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"apply\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batch_apply_ch\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Apply with BatchApplyCh: same prediction for the documented buffered configuration.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"barrier\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batch_apply_ch\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Barrier with the default unbuffered applyCh: every post-shutdown call answered, the contrast that the batched case is measured against.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"apply\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batch_apply_ch\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Apply with the default unbuffered applyCh: same contrast.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_shutdown_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\",\\\"kind\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"post_responded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"shutdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"kind\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"verify\\\"}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"VerifyLeader, whose channel is always buffered: the strand re-measured in the same run as the new cases.\\\"}]}}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
